-- Erdős #488, read from its sentence on erdosproblems.com for the Lean intake's F2 (lean/READING.md). Written by a model
-- session given only the sentence and lean/READING.md, told to use no tool (blind by instruction, not by sandbox),
-- 2026-11-10; kept as it replied, its comments included.
reading erdos-488
source  erdosproblems = corpus/intake/erdos-488/sentence.json
quote   from erdosproblems
proposed by model:claude-opus-5-5 (blind: given only the sentence and lean/READING.md)
-- "Let A be a finite set": the sentence does not say which numbers A holds
given   A : finite set of positive integers | finite set of naturals | finite set of integers
-- the sentence never gives n and m a domain ([1, n] and dividing by n suggest positive integers, but it does not say so)
given   n, m : positive integer | natural | integer
-- B = { n >= 1 : a | n for some a in A }; the bound variable is renamed x so it does not capture the given n
let     B = {x ≥ 1 : some a in A, a divides x}
-- "for every m > n >= max(A)", in the sentence's order
assume  m > n
assume  n ≥ max(A)
claim   |B ∩ [1, m]| / m < 2 · |B ∩ [1, n]| / n
